{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4624-1","published":"2026-10-12T07:29:19Z","modified":"2026-10-13T10:30:05.856272931Z","related":["CVE-2026-50248","CVE-2026-77860","CVE-2026-77955","CVE-2026-78227","CVE-2026-80225","CVE-2026-81634","CVE-2026-81642","CVE-2026-82717","CVE-2026-82720","CVE-2026-85501"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-50248","CVE-2026-77860","CVE-2026-77955","CVE-2026-78227","CVE-2026-80225","CVE-2026-81634","CVE-2026-81642","CVE-2026-82717","CVE-2026-82720","CVE-2026-85501"],"summary":"Security update for unbound","details":"This update for unbound fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-77860: 'serve-expired' can bypass Unbound 'wait-limit' (bsc#1280403).\n- CVE-2026-77955: Possible ZONEMD verification bypass window (bsc#1280404).\n- CVE-2026-78227: Use-after-free in DoQ stream output buffer on reset re-transmission (bsc#1280405).\n- CVE-2026-80225: Possible degradation of service from continuous queries on the same TCP/DoT connection (bsc#1280406).\n- CVE-2026-81634: Possible heap buffer overflow during DNSSEC canonicalization (bsc#1280409).\n- CVE-2026-81642: Heap buffer overflow and possible Remote Code Execution when digesting DNSKEY (bsc#1280411).\n- CVE-2026-82717: CNAME synthesis could lead to heap corruption (bsc#1280412).\n- CVE-2026-82720: Use-after-free in DoH stream cleanup code path (bsc#1280413).\n- CVE-2026-85501: Retrap: Novel Vulnerabilities to launch Algorithmic Complexity Attacks on DNSSEC (bsc#1280414).\n\nChanges for libunbound-devel-mini:\n\n- Updated to version 1.26.1\n\nChanges for unbound:\n\n- Updated to version 1.26.1\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"unbound","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/unbound&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.26.1-150100.10.31.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libunbound8":"1.26.1-150100.10.31.1","unbound-anchor":"1.26.1-150100.10.31.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source